From e28b9debfcf0cfdc5ad424704c170d3977811231 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mminin <mminin2010@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:30:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XFA: Decode PNG, BMP and TIFF images

Images in XFA forms were drawn only when they were JPEG or GIF. Every
form of the Canada Revenue Agency carries its logo as a PNG, and the
immigration forms use BMP and TIFF images.

The decoders move to XFAImage.cc. PNG, GIF, BMP and TIFF images are
decoded to 8-bit samples, with transparency as a soft mask instead of
being composited on white. Images with aspect="actual" are sized by
their resolution where the file gives one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
